WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:01.180
FEDERICO BONGIOVANNI:
Hello, everybody.

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:02.740
My name is Federico Bongiovanni.

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:05.110
I am an engineer and
manager here at Google.

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:08.310
I work in Google Cloud, and
specifically in Kubernetes.

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:11.580
I just finished my talk, which
was about an introduction

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.470
to SIG API Machinery.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:17.720
I am the co-chair of
the SIG API Machinery,

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.470
which is a central part
of Kubernetes clusters.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:22.990
As you know, all your
requests, anything that you

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:24.810
want to do with the
cluster is going

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.010
to come through our software.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.520
What are the parts of one
of Kubernetes that we own

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.770
and also what are the parts of
Kubernetes that we don't own?

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:34.250
Some people think
that because we

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:38.250
are called API Machinery we own
all the Kubernetes APIs, which

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.330
is not the right thing.

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.340
So yeah, I think was
a good talk to give

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.870
an overview of what we own.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:46.234
The other part of the talk was
about how you can get involved,

00:00:46.234 --> 00:00:49.080
if you want, into
open-source community,

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.070
and specifically in Kubernetes.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:54.090
API Machinery has
this fame of being

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:58.170
a super hard part of the
Kubernetes cluster, which

00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:58.860
is true.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:03.010
We have a big responsibility,
but it's not impossible.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.880
So I would love to see
some of you showing up

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:07.660
in our open-source meetings.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:11.770
So come, show up, learn,
listen, contribute, help us.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:13.410
I would also like
to invite all of you

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.742
to come to the
Google booths here.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:16.700
It's looking very good.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.030
So thank you very much.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:18.950
And see you soon.

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:22.300
[MUSIC PLAYING]

